<title>USA: Maine to spend part of surplus cash on tourism.</title>
<headline>Maine to spend part of surplus cash on tourism.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine's revenues are running ahead of estimates by more than $20 million, and Gov Angus King is expected to propose using $2.5 million for an increased tourism advertising campaign.</p>
<p>State Economic Development Commissioner Tom McBreaity said he convinced the governor that an investment in tourism advertising will generate more tourists and raise state revenues.</p>
<p>He added the campaign will be targeted to help all areas of the state, not just the coast.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
